/******************************************************************************
 * PFG_401K_PERIOD_DATES
 *
 * Type          : Extract Rule
 * Attached to   : Extract parameters "Period End Date" and "Check Date"
 * Returns       : L_PERIOD_END_DATE, L_CHECK_DATE
 *
 * Resolves which payroll period the run covers, from the payroll and the
 * effective date, rather than letting either be typed in.
 *
 * The reason is reruns. A file is identified at Principal's end by its
 * contract and its period end date, and our own duplicate guard keys on the
 * same pair. If the period were an operator-entered parameter, a rerun with
 * yesterday's effective date and this period's end date would produce a file
 * that looks like a period already delivered and is not - or, worse, one that
 * passes the duplicate check and posts a second set of repayments against a
 * period that was already settled.
 *
 * Deriving both dates from the payroll definition means the effective date is
 * the only thing an operator supplies, and any two runs for the same
 * effective date describe the same period.
 *
 * The period selected is the one whose end date is on or before the effective
 * date - the last period that has actually closed. Selecting the period the
 * effective date falls *inside* would pick up a period payroll has not yet
 * confirmed, and report repayments that have not been withheld.
 *****************************************************************************/

DEFAULT FOR PAY_PAYROLL_PERIOD_END_DATE IS '4712/12/31 00:00:00' (date)
DEFAULT FOR PAY_PAYROLL_PERIOD_DIRECT_DEPOSIT_DATE IS '4712/12/31 00:00:00' (date)
DEFAULT FOR PAY_PAYROLL_ACTION_STATUS IS 'U'

INPUTS ARE EFFECTIVE_DATE (date), PAYROLL_NAME (text)

L_PERIOD_END_DATE = PAY_PAYROLL_PERIOD_END_DATE
L_CHECK_DATE      = PAY_PAYROLL_PERIOD_DIRECT_DEPOSIT_DATE

/* Principal reconciles a repayment against the date the money reached the
   participant's bank, not the date the period ended. Where a payroll has no
   direct deposit date - an off-cycle paid by cheque - the period end date
   stands in, which is what Principal's profile asks for. */
IF L_CHECK_DATE = TO_DATE('4712/12/31', 'YYYY/MM/DD') THEN
(
  L_CHECK_DATE = L_PERIOD_END_DATE
)

/* An unconfirmed payroll has no run results worth extracting. Returning the
   end-of-time date makes that visible: the file's header carries 47121231,
   the canonical map passes it through, and it is caught in review rather than
   quietly delivering a period of zeros.

   This is deliberately not a formula error. An error here fails the whole
   extract with a message nobody can act on; an obviously wrong date in the
   header is diagnosable in one look. */
IF PAY_PAYROLL_ACTION_STATUS <> 'C' THEN
(
  L_PERIOD_END_DATE = TO_DATE('4712/12/31', 'YYYY/MM/DD')
  L_CHECK_DATE      = TO_DATE('4712/12/31', 'YYYY/MM/DD')
)

RETURN L_PERIOD_END_DATE, L_CHECK_DATE
